fix(hook): capture only what the stopping run wrote (#261)

git add -A staged the whole worktree, so a run became the signed author of
whatever else happened to be uncommitted. Measured three times on 2026-09-18:
a review subagent that had written nothing signed 12 files; a capture took
another agent's in-flight work, which that agent soft-reset and re-committed;
a third took a one-line edit the session made. Each verified against Fulcio and
Rekor under the wrong identity, which is worse than unsigned.

The bound is the run's own tool-call bodies, which name the files it wrote. A
run whose bodies cannot be read cannot say what it touched, so the capture
refuses and names the run to sign under later rather than claiming the tree.

